# Personal Book Library Web Application

This project is a frontend web application developed to manage a personal book library. It allows users to add, search, borrow, return, and manage books with a clean and interactive user interface.

The application is built using pure HTML, CSS, and JavaScript and stores data locally using the browser's LocalStorage. This project was developed as part of a Web Development Internship task.

---

## Features

- Add new books with title, author, category, and cover image
- Delete books (only when the book is not borrowed)
- Search books by title or author
- Filter books by category
- Borrow books using borrower ID and name
- Specify expected return duration while borrowing
- Return books with borrower ID verification
- Automatic fine calculation for late returns
- Maintain complete borrowing history for each book
- Dashboard showing total, borrowed, and available books
- Data persistence using LocalStorage
- Clean and responsive frontend design

---

## Project Rules and Logic

- A borrowed book cannot be deleted
- Borrower ID must match to return a book
- Fine is calculated as:  
  `(Number of late days × 50)`
- All application data is stored in the browser using LocalStorage
- No backend or database is used

